#
# smoke.expected -- what each console-producing image must print under QEMU.
# Read by `./x test qemu` (smoke.sh). Edit by hand, in the same commit as the
# change to the application that moves the text; unlike metrics.golden there is
# no `bless`, because a wrong string here would be blessed silently.
#
# One row per (image, string), TAB-separated:
#   image    the ELF, as a path relative to the repository root
#   string   a FIXED string (not a regexp) that must occur somewhere on the
#            guest console, i.e. what the program wrote to MMUART0. QEMU's own
#            messages go to stderr and are never searched. A line may be listed
#            several times for several strings; all must appear. Lines end in
#            CR LF on the wire, so do not anchor or include a line ending.
#
# Each image prints the id of the hart it runs on, read from mhartid, so the
# hart gate of start.S is checked as well: the E51 image runs on hart 0 only,
# the U54 image on hart 1 only.
#
# The pmp_probe rows record how many PMP entries (pmpaddr0 .. 15 that read back
# what was written) QEMU gives the harts of the icicle kit: 8 with QEMU 10.1.0,
# where the Renode model of the same board has 16. The rows are here so that a
# QEMU that changes the number fails the smoke test instead of going unnoticed.
image	string
examples/bare_hello/bin-e51/bare_hello.elf	bare hello E51 hart 0
examples/bare_hello/bin-u54/bare_hello.elf	bare hello U54 hart 1
examples/pmp_probe/bin-e51/pmp_probe.elf	pmp probe hart 0
examples/pmp_probe/bin-e51/pmp_probe.elf	pmp entries 8
examples/pmp_probe/bin-u54/pmp_probe.elf	pmp probe hart 1
examples/pmp_probe/bin-u54/pmp_probe.elf	pmp entries 8
